#94001
"Neatly Squared Cave"
"You are within a large room carved directly from the stone of the mountain.
Someone has obviously gone to a lot of effort to make the room perfectly
squared off as if it had been built of dressed stones rather than simply hewn
haphazardly from rock.  Unlike the walls, the ceiling and floor appear to be
made of heavily reinforced wooden platforms.  Thick chains connect the floor
to the ceiling in each of the four corners of the room.  The dominant feature
of this entire room appears to be a large lever set in a small wooden dais
built into the center of the floor.  An arch set into the southern wall
appears to be the only visible sign of exit from this room.
"
"need lever code for all elevator rooms
"
